Original commit body from db3dd0dbb602d5960817df8392d282ec815eb58d:

analyze/merge_producers.py runs in run_behavior_map at the top of Phase C —
after _relativize_ir_paths, before refine_frameworks — and folds two
anchored producers' records for one declaration into one Symbol. Until now
run_all_analyzers concatenated the tree-sitter `rust` and `rust_analyzer`
lists and every Phase-C reader saw two records per function.

Nothing in the pass is Rust-shaped. A record's producer is its
origin_run_id -> AnalysisRun.pass; the pairing key is each producer's
declared MergeAnchor (registry, §10): same path, equal name_key, token
inside item or item equal to item; merge_participants supplies the anchored
producers and its UndeclaredProducerError IS the refusal (propagated, not
caught). The incumbent is the non-scip backend (registry.incumbent_first;
ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS moves from the lint into the registry so there is one
home) — ADR-0057 §5's built-in until WI-hukuf makes it a config preference.

The merged record is the incumbent's copy with: an id minted from the
merged attributes (ADR-0036 — the grammar has no slot that could make it
differ, so it coincides with the incumbent's whenever incumbent-first
leaves every identity attribute the incumbent's; recorded in ADR §3);
the ITEM span (INV-lodum's cure for every merged record); origin = both
producers' pass ids, incumbent first; meta union with the incumbent winning
a shared key (the SCIP moniker survives); attributes only the other producer
observed filled in; origin_run_id = the pass's own producer-merge run
(catalog._BUILTIN_PIPELINE_PASS_IDS), appended only when it folded
something (the file-symbol synthesizer's convention; a run for a no-op pass
is the ADR-0056 question the owner reserved). Per merged record the §1
candidate set — attribute -> [(value, producers)] — is kept in memory
(MergedRecord.candidates) for WI-binis's slot. Edges: src/dst/derived_from
rewired, edge_key reset so deduplicate_edges collapses twins (§11);
usage-context symbol_ref rewired. A record with two candidate partners, or
a partner claimed twice, is left unmerged and reported. A single producer
is untouched, byte for byte.

The Python incumbent (py.py) declares its anchor — last "." segment, item
span — ahead of the second Python producer WI-nanom names, and so a plugin
backend can pair with it; the pipeline test relies on it.

